  "description": "IDUSEH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H40 Dy4 N24 O16,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.684-4.222 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.44-124.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C53H52Dy4N24O19. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
